{"kind":"request","text":"Lending library: compose and land the planner's build branch. The design is approved (checker report 78b4b447 at befcbe3b, Draft 5). As the planner's assert a42da3df said, this is composition, not a build from the note.\n\nBranch planner/lending-library-build, head d7be4107cf1588eab609be51a8ce1890d9e08dd1, from main d3f5aa74. It merges cleanly with main 6afbb5b5 (checked with git merge-tree). It carries the approved design note unchanged (notes/2026-10-13-lending-library.md, SHA256 571d1f9f…, the bytes the checker approved), so the note lands with it.\n\nWhat the branch holds:\n- examples/lending/: the lending definition, its canonical bytes and pin (sha256:439cd20e…); shelf.ts (a thing's page as markdown with members' text literal, checked against the site's renderer; every thing read from the record); demo-script.md; browser/ (model, request custody, gateway, invitation joining with a WebCrypto device key, IndexedDB storage, screens); scripts/assets.mjs.\n- packages/scope/src/lending.ts and lending-assets.ts (generated), and one line in worker.ts: the interface is served at /lending/.\n- packages/scope/test/lending.test.ts (real scopes, application cohort: the nine-step story and refusals, another member's return, the 64-thing bound, role lists that keep earlier actions, the gateway through a lost reply and a reload, a visitor joining membership 4 by invitation through a lost reply, restart, replay) and lending-route.test.ts.\n- Root vitest.config.ts and package.json: the lending project and its two typechecks.\nThe planner ran the gate once at tree 27804163 (the tree of commit 868060f6, before the note-only merge): typecheck clean, 1156 tests passed.\n\nWhat is NOT in the branch, and is not asked of this request:\n- Publishing a shelf page. The interface shows each page's text and says it is not published. Hugh is deciding between the browser edit of section 4.1 and publication from a fold (request bb47000e); do not build either here.\n- The screens and browser storage have not been run in a browser. Say so in the delivery note; do not claim them shown.\n- The runbook run on a deployed service, the online room, and the homepage Library page. These follow in their own requests.\nSo section 9's outputs 1 and 4 are delivered, output 2 is partly delivered, and outputs 3, 5 and 6 remain owed, with the publication-stage acceptance cases and the public history witness.\n\nOne deviation from the note to record: the site's renderer links a bare address (https://…, www.…, an email address) even in escaped text, so a member's text can hold such a link. It shows the address it goes to. The note's \"or a link\" is too strong; examples/lending/shelf.ts and its test say what holds.\n\nAlso for your judgement while composing: browser/custody.ts is a second request custody beside the Counter's, because the Counter's journal and device import accept only the counting definition. One shared module would be better; fold that into the consolidation (38064e13) if it fits, otherwise leave it and say so.","body":{"conditions":"Compose planner/lending-library-build at d7be4107 onto current main, under apps/ in the consolidated layout if that is where examples now live, changing only what the move needs (paths, imports, config, the generated assets module rebuilt with the assets script). Keep the definition's bytes and pin, the approved note's bytes, and every test's assertions. Run the gate once at the composed head. File the exact-head review to the checker with the design note's conditions as the review's conditions, stating plainly what is and is not delivered as listed in this request. Land on approval. Do not build page publication, the runbook, the room or the homepage page under this request. Priority: the demo head that follows the logo, as assert a42da3df set.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}